   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] Error:  No milestone data found for part(s) 1. Run this/these first before running part 2.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Hello Martine,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">As documented <a href=\"https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/readmyacccsv.html\" title=\"here\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/readmyacccsv.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488719740000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2T_peoCcF89GpMLK6yL1ku\">here</a>, always first try to run <span>read.myacc.csv() on its own before providing the parameters values to the GGIR() function. By doing so you can test that your parameter values are correct by check that the output of the function is correct.</span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><span><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><span>For example, I think timezone is reference with %Z and not with %OS, but you should find out quickly if you follow that approach. </span><a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" href=\"https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/~s133/dates.html\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/~s133/dates.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488719740000&amp;usg=AOvVaw26mQ7C9A28zVnmLVtG2EJy\">https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/~s133/dates.html</a></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Please note that even though you have the timezone there and should specify it, GGIR ignores this when actually processing the timestamps. Additionally, you always have to specify parameter <a href=\"https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/GGIRParameters.html#desiredtz\" title=\"desiredtz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/GGIRParameters.html%23desiredtz&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488719740000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3jj_wC82-V3IwUAvEFHMHO\">desiredtz</a> to indicate the timezone your data was collected in, unless it is the timezone your computer is in, in which case you can keep the default value of &quot;&quot;. If your recording was configured in a different timezone also consider parameter <a href=\"https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/GGIRParameters.html#configtz\" title=\"configtz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/GGIRParameters.html%23configtz&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488719740000&amp;usg=AOvVaw13UNipv6pQk2yftOrTW0Ey\">configtz</a>. These parameters ensure that day saving time is correctly accounted for.</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><span><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"></div><blockquote style=\"border-left:3px solid rgb(200,200,200);border-top-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-right-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-bottom-color:rgb(200,200,200);padding-left:10px;color:rgb(102,102,102)\"><div style=\"line-height:1.5;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">I also tryed using Actigraph datas from testifies <a href=\"https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR/blob/master/inst/testfiles/ActiGraph13.csv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR/blob/master/inst/testfiles/ActiGraph13.csv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488719740000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JWOFDwG9BRoVkHCxIPjqK\">https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR/blob/master/inst/testfiles/ActiGraph13.csv</a> but it didn&#39;t work.</font></div></blockquote><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">That does not work because it is not raw accelerometer data, but count data. The functionality  only works for raw data (multiple values per second).</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Best,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Vincent</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(107,107,107)\">Dr. Vincent van Hees | Independent consultant | </span><a title=\"https://accelting.com/\" href=\"https://accelting.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://accelting.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488719740000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1kwjJ_vfyjrpr6uBWiUGuc\">https://accelting.com/</a><br></div><div><img alt=\"image\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/RpackageGGIR/attach/1a035ad4430c5/image?part=0.1.1&amp;view=1\"><br></div>\r\n    </div>\r\n    \r\n            <div>\r\n        \r\n            </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div></div>"
